Boot even when the database is unreachable

The API stopped answering entirely: /api/health returned zero bytes until the
client timed out. init_db() ran synchronously in the lifespan, so a failed
connection raised before uvicorn began listening - the platform health check
never got an answer and the site just hung, with the real cause visible only in
the logs.

- init_db_safe() catches the failure, logs it, and lets startup continue
- connect_timeout=10 so an unreachable host fails fast instead of hanging
- /api/storage/status now reports database_ready + database_error
- a background task retries the schema every 30s, so a resumed database heals
  itself without a redeploy
- the startup banner states where files really go (it claimed "local disk"
  even when blobs were stored in Postgres)

Verified against a bogus tenant: the server boots, /api/health answers in 2.3s
and /api/storage/status returns durable=false with "tenant/user ... not found".
